Interactive USD edits of an ArnoldOptions prim, with the render delegate

A grey sphere lit by a distant light is rendered by the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra
host, with an ArnoldOptions prim whose ignore_lights attribute is enabled. It is disabled, enabled again and removed.
The stage is re-rendered after each edit. Covers the fix of the options updates restarting the render (#2666), which
can't be seen yet: with hydra 1 the edits of the options prim aren't applied, with hydra 2 the prim isn't applied at
all (known issues in test.cpp). See testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and
the last render is compared against the reference image.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
